{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 67, :comments ["<b>ויבאה</b> Two times in the Masorah in the book of Genesis. Written defective and equals 24, teaching that she adorned herself with 24 adornments:" "<b>האהלה</b> Eight times in the Masorah. A hint that in eight places the Shekhinah dwelled: Mishkan, Gilgal, Shiloh, Nov, Giv'on, First Temple, Second Temple, in the time to come:" "<b>ותהי לו</b> for a wife, and Abraham again took. Proper conduct: one whose wife died and left him sons — he marries them off before he takes another wife. Another interpretation: this is what they said: שתין תכלי מטי׳ לככא דקל חבריה שמע דאכיל ואיהו לא אכיל:" "<b>ויאהבה</b> Two times in the Masorah: here and the other ויאהבה אמנון. There the love was dependent on something, therefore it was nullified; but here it is not dependent on something, therefore it was not nullified:" "<b>וינחם</b> Two times in the Masorah: וינחם יצחק, and וינחם כרוב חסדיו. Why was וינחם יצחק followed by כרוב חסדיו? Meaning that she was righteous and pious:"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {2 "The Aramaic proverb is rendered exactly as it appears; it appears to be a popular saying about a date palm whose companion eats while he himself does not eat, but the text is left untranslated as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:57.518488332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}